BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:script-pipeline-first-look-project-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Script Pipeline: First Look Project 2026 (screenplay and 
 TV pilot contest)
DESCRIPTION:The 15th annual First Look Project from Script Pipeline searche
 s for higher-concept material across six categories: feature screenplays i
 n Action and Sci-Fi\, Comedy\, Drama\, and Horror and Thriller\, plus hour
  and half-hour original TV pilots. Unlike Script Pipeline's Screenwriting 
 and TV Writing contests\, entries are judged on both writing ability and m
 arket potential\, in addition to originality of concept\; a script that st
 ill needs refining can win if the story could stand out in the current lan
 dscape\, as the aim is a first look at the next buzzworthy specs before th
 ey hit the market. GUIDELINES: screenplays must be feature length\; genres
  without a listed category go to the closest one (Fantasy\, Western or Adv
 enture under Action and Sci-Fi\; Crime and Mystery under Thriller). TV pil
 ots run roughly 30 to 60 pages\, all genres accepted including animation a
 nd genre hybrids. The script must not be under an option or shopping agree
 ment at the time of entry\, and the same script cannot compete in multiple
  categories. CIRCULATION: Script Pipeline's industry relationships (Bellev
 ue Productions\, LBI Entertainment\, Hungry Man\, Alibi Management and oth
 ers) have led to writers signed\, specs sold and films produced. Regular d
 eadline 30 September 2026\; late deadline 15 October\; extended deadline 3
 0 October. Winners announced 15 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Script Pip
 eline\nLocation: Online submission\; open to writers worldwide. Script Pip
 eline is based in Los Angeles\, US.\nAward: USD 15\,000 in total prizes ac
 ross six winners: USD 2\,500 to the winner of each of four screenplay genr
 e categories (Action and Sci-Fi\, Comedy\, Drama\, Horror and Thriller) an
 d USD 2\,500 to the winner of each of two TV pilot categories (hour and ha
 lf-hour). All winners also receive long-term circulation to Script Pipelin
 e's industry network of producers\, managers\, agents and directors\, 1-on
 -1 development assistance from Script Pipeline execs\, additional script r
 eviews and consideration of other material\, career guidance and mentorshi
 p\, and invitations to private Symposium events. Entry fee: USD 60 at the 
 regular deadline\, rising to USD 65 (late\, 15 October) and USD 70 (extend
 ed\, 30 October).\nDuration: Winners announced 15 December 2026.\n\nMore: 
 https://scriptpipeline.com/contest/first-look-project?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://scriptpipeline.com/contest/first-look-project?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission\; open to writers worldwide. Script Pipeline is 
 based in Los Angeles\, US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rome-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Rome: Rome Prize Fellowship 2027-28
DESCRIPTION:The Rome Prize supports roughly 30 artists and scholars a year 
 with a residential fellowship at the American Academy in Rome\; discipline
 s include Design and Visual Arts\, where media and new-genre work is regul
 arly funded. Fellows receive a USD 16\,000 (half-term) or USD 30\,000 (ful
 l-term) stipend plus housing\, workspace and weekday meals on the Academy'
 s Janiculum campus. ELIGIBILITY: US citizens for most categories\; foreign
  nationals who have lived in the US for the three years preceding the dead
 line may apply in Environmental Arts and Humanities and certain postdoctor
 al categories. FEES: USD 50 (one category) or USD 60 (multiple) by 1 Novem
 ber 2026\; a late window runs to 15 November at USD 80/90. DEADLINE: 1 Nov
 ember 2026.\n\nOrganisation: American Academy in Rome\nLocation: Rome\, It
 aly (residential fellowship at the Academy\; US organisation with NYC offi
 ce). RESTRICTED: US citizens for most categories\; foreign nationals resid
 ent in the US for the 3 years preceding the deadline may apply only in cer
 tain categories.\nAward: Stipends of USD 16\,000 (half-term\, about 5 mont
 hs) and USD 30\,000 (full-term\, about 10 months)\, plus housing\, workspa
 ce and weekday meals. Approximately 30 fellowships per year. APPLICATION F
 EE: USD 50 by 1 November (USD 60 for multiple categories)\; USD 80/90 in t
 he late window to 15 November.\nDuration: 5 or 10 months\n\nMore: https://
 www.aarome.org/apply/rome-prize?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.aarome.org/apply/rome-prize?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rome\, Italy (residential fellowship at the Academy\; US organisat
 ion with NYC office). RESTRICTED: US citizens for most categories\; foreig
 n nationals resident in the US for the 3 years preceding the deadline may 
 apply only in certain categories.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vsa-emerging-young-artists-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261120
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kennedy Center: Access/VSA Emerging Young Artists 2027\, 
 Thrive (15 x USD 3\,000)
DESCRIPTION:The Kennedy Center's Access/VSA Emerging Young Artists Program 
 (2027 theme: Thrive) awards 15 young disabled visual artists a USD 3\,000 
 stipend\, an all-expenses-paid career development week in Washington DC (1
 4 to 18 June 2027) and exhibition of one work. ELIGIBILITY: aged 16 to 25 
 on the deadline date\; US-based with the right to work in the US\; have a 
 disability as defined by the ADA and be willing to disclose it publicly\; 
 submitted work made in the last three years and after the onset of disabil
 ity\; no generative-AI work\; previous winners ineligible. OBLIGATIONS: at
 tend three virtual workshops (April to June 2027) and the DC week to recei
 ve the stipend. APPLICATION: free\, via CaFE (artist.callforentry.org)\; a
 ccommodation and alternative-format requests by 30 October 2026. Winners n
 otified by 13 January 2027. Questions: vsainfo@kennedy-center.org. DEADLIN
 E: 19 November 2026\, 23:59 ET.\n\nOrganisation: John F. Kennedy Center fo
 r the Performing Arts\, Office of Accessibility and VSA\nLocation: USA (50
  states\, DC\, Puerto Rico and territories\; right to work in the US requi
 red). Career week and exhibition in Washington DC.\nAward: 15 winners each
  receive a USD 3\,000 stipend\, an all-expenses-paid career development we
 ek in Washington DC (14 to 18 June 2027)\, and exhibition of one work in D
 C. No entry fee.\nDuration: Three virtual workshops April to June 2027\, D
 C week 14 to 18 June 2027\, then the exhibition.\n\nMore: https://opportun
 ities.wearecreativewest.org/opportunity/17971/CAFE?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opportunities.wearecreativewest.org/opportunity/17971/CAFE?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA (50 states\, DC\, Puerto Rico and territories\; right to work 
 in the US required). Career week and exhibition in Washington DC.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oregon-media-arts-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Oregon Media Arts Fellowship 2026 (two USD 5\,000 awards 
 for Oregon media artists)
DESCRIPTION:The Oregon Media Arts Fellowship\, run by the Portland Art Muse
 um's Center for an Untold Tomorrow with the Oregon Arts Commission\, gives
  Oregon media artists money to create or complete new work. Eligible work 
 is artist-driven moving image\, sound\, digital or time-based media: narra
 tive\, documentary and experimental film\, animation\, video art\, artist-
 made television\, audio and podcasts\, immersive and interactive media\, w
 eb-based and digital work\, AR\, VR and mixed reality\, and emerging forms
 . Review criteria include sustained professional achievement and potential
  future contribution to the field. ELIGIBILITY: artists aged 18 or over wh
 o have lived in Oregon for at least one year as their fixed\, permanent pr
 incipal home\, not enrolled in a creative degree programme\, and who have 
 not received a Media Arts Fellowship or any Oregon Arts Commission fellows
 hip in the previous five years\; one application per year\, joint applicat
 ions split a single award. DEADLINE: 15 November 2026 (no time stated\; la
 te applications are not guaranteed processing).\n\nOrganisation: Portland 
 Art Museum (PAM CUT) and Oregon Arts Commission\nLocation: Oregon\, United
  States (Oregon residents only).\nAward: Two fellowships of USD 5\,000 eac
 h\, no matching funds required\; paid within two months of notification. N
 o application fee.\nDuration: One-time award for new work or works in prog
 ress.\n\nMore: https://portlandartmuseum.org/artist-services/oregon-media-
 arts-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/artist-services/oregon-media-arts-fellows
 hip/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Oregon\, United States (Oregon residents only).
END:VEVENT
